  "body": "Fixes #331296\n\nRelated to #194322 and #331139.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Treat `ProcessItem.mem` consistently as bytes when formatting the `code --status` process table.\n- Document the byte-valued `ProcessItem.mem` contract.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`listProcesses` already converts non-Windows `%mem` values to bytes, but `DiagnosticsService.formatProcessItem` applied the old percentage-to-bytes calculation a second time on macOS and Linux. This produced impossible values such as 25,332,747,904 MB for a process with about 94 MiB RSS.\n\nThe Process Explorer already formats `item.mem` as bytes. This change makes the diagnostics text path consistent with that behavior.\n\nPR #331139 changes the macOS source metric from RSS to physical footprint but continues to store the result in bytes, so the two fixes are compatible and address separate output paths.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Reproduced on VS Code 1.133.0, macOS 26.5.1 arm64.\n- TypeScript syntax transpile passed for both changed files.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- Confirmed the patch applies cleanly to current `main` at `4ccdb71a3e5`.",
  "rebaseable": true
 },
